# Copy to .devcontainer/devcontainer.env (GITIGNORED — see the repo's .gitignore) and fill in.
#
# Passed to `docker run` via the "runArgs": ["--env-file", ...] in devcontainer.json, so it
# is picked up automatically at container start. Nothing needs to be exported in the shell
# that launched VS Code, and none of it is baked into an image layer.

# Your PUBLIC signing key — the single line from `cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_sk.pub` on the HOST.
# This is the .pub file. A public key is NOT a secret; the private half stays on the YubiKey
# and never enters the container. The feature refuses a value that looks like a private key.
#
# You also need the key loaded in the HOST's ssh-agent, or commits fail to sign:
#     ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519_sk
#     ssh-add -l          # should list it
SSH_SIGNING_PUBKEY=
